      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update dotnet8-runtime to 8.0.32-r0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-70181 (GHSA-w5qq-qrpp-rf4c) is an ASP.NET Core denial of service issue: FileBufferingReadStream in Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities eagerly rents buffers during multipart processing, which allows memory exhaustion. Microsoft lists the ASP.NET Core 8.0 runtime packs, including linux-musl-x64 and linux-musl-arm64, as affected from 8.0.0 through 8.0.31 and fixed in 8.0.32 (https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w5qq-qrpp-rf4c, https://github.com/dotnet/announcements/issues/459, https://github.com/dotnet/core/blob/main/release-notes/8.0/8.0.32/8.0.32.md). DHI dotnet8-runtime for Alpine 3.23 builds .NET 8 for Linux from Microsoft's source release, and each build's version is the .NET runtime version it carries. Scanned all 220 packages of the ten published builds (8.0.23-r0, 8.0.24-r0, 8.0.25-r0, 8.0.26-r0, 8.0.27-r0, 8.0.29-r0, 8.0.31-r0, 8.0.32-r0, 8.0.33-r0 and 8.0.34-r0) for x86_64 and aarch64, including the files inside the nupkg and other zip archives they hold: every build ships Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities.dll at its own .NET version, in the ASP.NET Core shared framework of aspnetcore8-runtime and of the .NET SDK held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap, in the ASP.NET Core runtime pack held by dotnet8-runtime-bootstrap, and in the Microsoft.AspNetCore.WebUtilities nupkg in dotnet8-runtime-artifacts, plus reference assemblies with no implementation code (including 6.0.2 reference assemblies in source-build reference packages): 8.0.23 to 8.0.31 in the first seven builds and 8.0.32 or later from 8.0.32-r0 on. The range ends at 8.0.32-r0 because it is the first published build with the fix."
    },
